gives guidance on","tree_line_end":291,"tree_line_start":287},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1.\n the Social Security (Coronavirus) (Further Measures) Regulations\n1\n which came into force on \n30.3.20 \nand","tree_line_end":305,"tree_line_start":292},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"2.\n \nthe Universal Credit (Extension of Coronavirus Measures) Regulations\n2\n which came into force \non 6.4.21.","tree_line_end":318,"tree_line_start":306},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" \n \n \n \n1 SS (Coronavirus) (Further Measures) Regs;\n \nSI 2020 No. 371\n;\n \n2 UC (Ext of Coronavirus \nMeasures) Regs; \nSI 2021 No. 313","tree_line_end":340,"tree_line_start":319},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"2.\n \nThe regulations cease to have effect on","tree_line_end":347,"tree_line_start":341},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1.\n 31.7.21 for those provisions included in the guidance about the minimum income floor at \nparagraphs 4 – 6\n1\nand","tree_line_end":360,"tree_line_start":348},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"2.\n \n31.8.21 for those provisions included in the guidance about JSA periods of sickness at \nparagraphs 16\n \n– 20\n2\n.","tree_line_end":374,"tree_line_start":361},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 SS (Coronavirus) (Further Measures) Regs, reg 10(2A); 2 reg 10(2B)\n ","tree_line_end":381,"tree_line_start":375},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"3. The regulations","tree_line_end":386,"tree_line_start":382},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1.\n give the Secretary of State discretion to apply a number of measures in relation to the minimum \nincome floor (MIF) for self-employed UC claimants","tree_line_end":394,"tree_line_start":387},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"2.\n modify the amount of the standard allowance in UC","tree_line_end":401,"tree_line_start":395},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"3.\n dis-apply the application of periods of sickness in JSA for those affected by Coronavirus \ndisease.","tree_line_end":409,"tree_line_start":402},{"depth":2,"role":"H3","text":"UC: MINIMUM INCOOR FLOOR (MIF)","tree_line_end":415,"tree_line_start":410},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"4.\n \n The MIF normally applies from the start of the award or at the end of the start-up period to UC \nclaimants who\n1","tree_line_end":426,"tree_line_start":416},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1. \nare gainfully self-employed \nand","tree_line_end":435,"tree_line_start":427},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"2.\n would otherwise fall within the all work-related requirements group.","tree_line_end":442,"tree_line_start":436},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"Note:\n See \nChapter H4 \n(Earned income – self-employed earnings) for detailed guidance on the MIF, \nand \nChapter J2\n (Work related groups) for guidance on work-related requirements.","tree_line_end":460,"tree_line_start":443},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 UC Regs, reg 62","tree_line_end":467,"tree_line_start":461},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"5. \n \n From 30.3.20 the DM has discretion to apply a number of measures in relation to the MIF for self-\nemployed claimants as a consequence of the outbreak of Coronavirus disease.","tree_line_end":475,"tree_line_start":468},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"6.\n \n The measures allow the DM to\n1","tree_line_end":485,"tree_line_start":476},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1.\n treat the amount of the individual or couple threshold\n2\n as if it were a lesser amount (including nil)","tree_line_end":496,"tree_line_start":486},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"2.\n delay making a determination as to whether a claimant is in gainful self-employment\n3","tree_line_end":506,"tree_line_start":497},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"3.\n \n \nwhere it has already been determined that the claimant is in gainful self-employment, treat the \nclaimant as not being in gainful self-employment\n ","tree_line_end":517,"tree_line_start":507},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"4.\n where a claimant is in a start-up period\n4\n, extend that period for as long as considered \nappropriate","tree_line_end":529,"tree_line_start":518},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"5. \nwhere a self-employed claimant would otherwise fall within the all work-related requirements \ngroup\n5\n, except the claimant from a work search requirement\n6\n or a work availability requirement\n7\n.","tree_line_end":549,"tree_line_start":530},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 SS (Coronavirus) (Further Measures) Regs, reg 2; 2 UC Regs, reg 62(4) and 90(2) & (3); 3 reg 64; 4\n \nreg 63;\n5 WR Act 12, s 22; 6 s 17; 7 s 18","tree_line_end":561,"tree_line_start":550},{"depth":2,"role":"H3","text":"UC: STANDARD ALLOWANCE AMOUNTS","tree_line_end":567,"tree_line_start":562},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"7.\n \n Guidance on the UC standard allowance amounts for the purpose of the maximum amount is at \nE2173\n.","tree_line_end":579,"tree_line_start":568},{"depth":2,"role":"H4","text":"CHANGES FROM 6.4.20","tree_line_end":585,"tree_line_start":580},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"8. The amounts are increased from the first day of the first assessment period which commences on \nor after 6.4.20\n1\n – see \nMemo ADM 03/20 \nfor details and where to find the amounts.","tree_line_end":600,"tree_line_start":586},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 SI 2020 No. 234","tree_line_end":607,"tree_line_start":601},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"9. The amounts for the purpose of any case affected by the Coronavirus\n \nfurther measures are to be \nread as if they were\n1\n:","tree_line_end":619,"tree_line_start":608},{"depth":2,"role":"Table","text":"Standard allowance\nAmou\nnt\nSingle claimant under 25\n£342.\n72\nSingle claimant 25 or over\n£409.\n89\nJoint claimants both under 25\n£488.\n59\nJoint claimants where either is 25 or \nover\n£594.\n04","tree_line_end":736,"tree_line_start":620},{"depth":3,"role":"TR","text":"Standard allowance\nAmou\nnt","tree_line_end":651,"tree_line_start":628},{"depth":4,"role":"TD","text":"Standard allowance","tree_line_end":639,"tree_line_start":630},{"depth":5,"role":"P","text":"Standard allowance","tree_line_e