":917},{"depth":5,"role":"P","text":"Joint claimants where either is 25 or \nover","tree_line_end":926,"tree_line_start":921},{"depth":4,"role":"TD","text":"£596.\n58","tree_line_end":936,"tree_line_start":927},{"depth":5,"role":"P","text":"£596.\n58","tree_line_end":936,"tree_line_start":931},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 UC (Ext of Coronavirus\n \nMeasures) Regs, reg 2(1)","tree_line_end":945,"tree_line_start":937},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"10.\n \n These amounts apply to awards of UC for any assessment period which ends","tree_line_end":952,"tree_line_start":946},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1. \non or after 6.4.21 \nand","tree_line_end":961,"tree_line_start":953},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"2. \nbefore 6.10.21\n1\n.","tree_line_end":972,"tree_line_start":962},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 UC (Ext of Coronavirus\n \nMeasures) Regs, reg 2(1)","tree_line_end":982,"tree_line_start":973},{"depth":2,"role":"H4","text":"TRANSITIONAL ELEMENT","tree_line_end":988,"tree_line_start":983},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"14. \nChapter M7\n (Managed migration pilot and Transitional protection) gives guidance on the","tree_line_end":998,"tree_line_start":989},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1. \ncalculation of the indicative UC amount for the purposes of determining any entitlement to the \ntransitional element\n1\nand","tree_line_end":1011,"tree_line_start":999},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"2.\n initial amount of the transitional element\n2\nand","tree_line_end":1023,"tree_line_start":1012},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"3.\n reduction of the initial amount by relevant increases\n3\n.","tree_line_end":1034,"tree_line_start":1024},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 UC (TP) Regs, reg 54; 2 reg 55(1) & (2)(a); 3 reg 55(2)(b), (c) & (4)","tree_line_end":1041,"tree_line_start":1035},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"15. When calculating any of the amounts in paragraph 14, the modified amounts in paragraphs 9 and \n12 are disregarded. The amounts referred to in \nE2173\n and the uprated amounts referred to in \nMemo \nADM 03/20 \nor \nMemo ADM 05/21\n apply instead\n1\n.","tree_line_end":1069,"tree_line_start":1042},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 SS (Coronavirus) (Further Measures) Regs, reg 3(3);\n \nUC (Ext of Coronavirus\n \nMeasures) Regs, reg 2(2)","tree_line_end":1082,"tree_line_start":1070},{"depth":2,"role":"H3","text":"JSA: PERIODS OF SICKNESS","tree_line_end":1088,"tree_line_start":1083},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"16. Where a JSA claimant","tree_line_end":1093,"tree_line_start":1089},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1. \nis affected by Coronavirus disease as in paragraph 18 below and","tree_line_end":1100,"tree_line_start":1094},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"2.\n satisfies the JSA conditions of entitlement apart from the condition that they do not have LCW\n1","tree_line_end":1110,"tree_line_start":1101},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"they are treated as not having LCW\n2\n.","tree_line_end":1119,"tree_line_start":1111},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" \n \n \n \n \nNote: \nSee \nADM Chapter R2\n (JSA conditions of entitlement) for guidance on short and extended \nperiods of sickness.","tree_line_end":1137,"tree_line_start":1120},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 JS Act 95 s1(2); 2 SS (Coronavirus) (Further Measures) Regs, reg 8(1)","tree_line_end":1144,"tree_line_start":1138},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"17. Any period where paragraph 16 applies is disregarded for the purposes of calculating short periods \nand extended period of sickness\n1\n.","tree_line_end":1154,"tree_line_start":1145},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 JSA Regs 13, reg 46(3) & 46A(5); SS (Coronavirus) (Further Measures) Regs, reg 8(2)","tree_line_end":1161,"tree_line_start":1155},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"18. A person is affected by Coronavirus disease if they are\n1","tree_line_end":1169,"tree_line_start":1162},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1.\n infected or contaminated with Coronavirus disease (also known as COVID-19) \nor","tree_line_end":1178,"tree_line_start":1170},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"2. \nin isolation (see paragraphs 19 – 20 below) \nor","tree_line_end":1187,"tree_line_start":1179},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"3.\n caring for a child or qualifying young person\n2\n who is a member of the person’s household and \nwho is","tree_line_end":1199,"tree_line_start":1188},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"3.1\n in isolation \nor","tree_line_end":1208,"tree_line_start":1200},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"3.2 \ninfected or contaminated with Coronavirus disease.","tree_line_end":1215,"tree_line_start":1209},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"Note:\n For the purposes of \n3.\n, a child or qualifying young person is a member of the person’s \nhousehold if they live with the person caring for them.","tree_line_end":1226,"tree_line_start":1216},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 SS (Coronavirus) (Further Measures) Regs, reg 8(2); 2 SS C&B Act 92, s. 142","tree_line_end":1233,"tree_line_start":1227},{"depth":2,"role":"H4","text":"MEANING OF \"ISOLATION\"","tree_line_end":1238,"tree_line_start":1234},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"19. A person is in isolation if they are separate from any other person so as to prevent infection or \ncontamination with Coronavirus disease\n1\n. DMs should have regard to the latest UK Government \nadvice to the public on when they should self-isolate on a case by case basis.","tree_line_end":1249,"tree_line_start":1239},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"Note:\n A person can be in isolation when they live with other people such as family members or in \nmultiple occupancy dwellings.","tree_line_end":1257,"tree_line_start":1250},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 SS (Coronavirus) (Further Measures) Regs, reg 1(2)","tree_line_end":1264,"tree_line_start":1258},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"20. This does not include where a person","tree_line_end":1269,"tree_line_start":1265},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1. \nhas not been advised to isolate \nor","tree_line_end":1278,"tree_line_start":1270},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"2. \nis looking after a child or qualifying young person whose school or nursery has been closed \nor","tree_line_end":1287,"tree_line_start":1279},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"3.\n is following UK Government advice on social distancing.","tree_line_end":1294,"tree_line_start":1288},{"depth":2,"role":"H3","text":" ","tree_line_end":1299,"tree_line_start":1295},{"depth":2,"role":"H3","text":"ANNOTATIONS","tree_line_end":1305,"tree_line_start":1300},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"Please annotate the number of this memo (ADM Memo 04/20) against the following ADM paragraphs \nand memos","tree_line_end":1310,"tree_line_start":1306},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"E2173\n, \nH4020 main heading\n, \nH4060 main heading\n, \nH4100 main heading\n, \nM7470\n, \nM7500 heading\n; \nR2942\n, \nR2957","tree_line_end":1352,"tree_line_start":1311},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"Memo ADM 03/20\n, \nMemo ADM 05/21","tree_line_end":1364,"tree_line_start":1353},{"depth":2,"role":"H3","text":" ","tree_line_end":1369,"tree_line_start":1365},{"depth":2,"role":"H3","text":"CONTACTS","tree_line_end":1375,"tree_line_start":1370},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"If you have any queries about this memo, please write to Decision Making and Appeals (DMA) Leeds, 3E \nzone E, Quarry House, Leeds. Existing arrangements for such referrals should be followed, as set out in – \nMemo \n7/19\n Requesting case guidance from DMA Leeds for all benefits.","tree_line_end":1386,"tree_line_start":1376},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" ","tree_line_end":1390,"tree_line_start":1387},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"DMA Leeds: July\n \n2021","tree_line_end":1399,"tree_line_start":1391},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" ","tree_line_end":1403,"tree_line_start":1400},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" ","tree_line_end":1407,"tree_line_start":1404},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"The content of the examples in this document (including use of imagery) is for illustrative purposes \nonly","tree_line_end":1413,"tree_line_start":1408}